# Renovate's Forgejo credential — template for nixos/renovate.sops.env.
# Fill, then: sops -e -i nixos/renovate.sops.env
#
# A .sops.env rather than a key in secrets.sops.yaml, deliberately: adding a
# key to an already-encrypted sops-yaml needs the age PRIVATE key (the MAC is
# recomputed over every value), and nixos/secrets.sops.yaml holds real ed25519
# private halves — so "regenerate it from the .example" would destroy them.
# Creating a NEW file needs only the public recipient. The content is consumed
# WHOLE as a systemd EnvironmentFile by one unit, which is exactly the
# criterion CLAUDE.md gives for dotenv. nixos/modules/ci-secrets.nix decrypts
# it into /run/ci-secrets/renovate.env with the host age key.

# Forgejo PAT
# For the Renovate bot user. Scopes (Forgejo 16 model): read:user, write:issue,
# write:repository — nothing more. This is for Renovate's OWN API calls and
# must NEVER be used by a workflow to push (see the loop-prevention comment in
# .forgejo/workflows/renovate-pins.yml). Until it is filled, ci-secrets.nix
# writes no runtime file and renovate.service is SKIPPED, not failed.
#   Forgejo -> Settings -> Applications -> Generate New Token
#   sopsedit nixos/renovate.sops.env
#   nixos-rebuild switch --target-host idan@10.0.0.3 --use-remote-sudo --flake .#services-vm
RENOVATE_TOKEN=changeme_forgejo_renovate_pat
